      ],
      "explanation": "We do not need to find \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) separately. The even powers have the same values at \\(3\\) and \\(-3\\), so subtracting the two function values eliminates both unknown coefficients:\n\\[\nf(3)=81a-9b+8,\n\\]\n\\[\nf(-3)=81a-9b+2.\n\\]\nThus\n\\[\nf(3)-f(-3)=6.\n\\]\nSince \\(f(-3)=2\\), we obtain \\(f(3)=2+6=\\boxed{8}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\).",
      "id": "cancel-even-powers",
